N`, the value must be either `GLFW_TRUE` to enable raw (unscaled and unaccelerated) mouse motion when the cursor is disabled, or `GLFW_FALSE` to disable it. If raw motion is not supported, attempting to set this will emit GLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE. Call glfwRawMouseMotionSupported to check for support.

  Args:
    window: The window whose input mode to set.
    mode: One of `GLFW_CURSOR`, `GLFW_STICKY_KEYS`, `GLFW_STICKY_MOUSE_BUTTONS`, `GLFW_LOCK_KEY_MODS` or `GLFW_RAW_MOUSE_MOTION`.
    value: The new value of the specified input mode.

